Protocol references

- kind3r/ttlock-sdk-js, https://github.com/kind3r/ttlock-sdk-js
  License: GPL-3.0. Primary reference for the TTLock Bluetooth LE protocol.
  Code ported from it to C++ keeps its GPL-3.0 terms and credits it in the
  ported file: in components/ttlock, the frame codec, the advertisement
  parser, the command builders and parsers, and the session flows.
  tools/vectors/kind3r_vectors.ts runs its command classes (commit 8c84cda)
  to generate test vectors.

- roquerodrigo/ttlock-ble, https://github.com/roquerodrigo/ttlock-ble
  Copyright (c) 2026 Rodrigo Roque. License: MIT. Second reference, used
  to cross-check commands and frames and, through
  tools/vectors/gen_vectors.py, to generate test vectors. Some parts of
  components/ttlock follow its code, and each such file says so: the CRC
  table quirk, the dormant advertisement bit, the passcode and card
  listing layouts, the feature words, the operation-log record types, the
  push events, and matching replies on the echoed opcode. Those parts are
  used under its MIT license:

